  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nNorthwest flow aloft with high pressure of Canadian origin building \nsoutheast thru the Ohio Valley today. Dry and Cool conditions will \npersist. The clear skies and light winds was leading to fog \ndevelopment especially in river valleys this morning. The fog will \nimprove quickly after sunrise with seasonably cool highs in the mid \nto upper 60s. \n\nTemperatures warm above normal Wednesday as southerly flow develops\nahead of the approach of a weak front. Highs on Wednesday are expect\nto range from 75 to 80. The weak front will drop into the area \nWednesday night/early Thursday - but limited moisture will lead to \njust some clouds with no rain expected. Another area of high \npressure builds in from the northwest during the second half of the \nweek.\n\nMid level ridging building into the area will allow for continued \ndry conditions late this week into Saturday with temperatures again\nwarming to 75 to 80 Saturday.  \n\nRain chances increase on Sunday into Monday when moisture from the \nGulf States advects north into the Ohio Valley ahead of a  midlevel \ntrough.",
